window.SOURATE_DATA = {"numSourate":27,"nomSourate":"An-Naml","nomFr":"Les fourmis","nomEn":"The Ant","nomArabe":"النمل","lieu":"La Mecque","lieuEn":"Makkah","typeSourateLabel":"Sourate Mecquoise","typeSourateLabelEn":"Meccan Surah","typeSourateClasse":"mecquoise","ordreRev":48,"nbVersets":93,"versets":[{"numVerset":1,"texteArabe":"بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ طس  تِلْكَ آيَاتُ الْقُرْآنِ وَكِتَابٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"T'â, Sîn. Voici les versets du Coran et d'un Livre explicite,","tradEn":"Ṭā, Seen. These are the verses of the Qur’ān [i.e., recitation] and a clear Book","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ṭâ, Sîn: Ces lettres isolées placées en ouverture de la sourate appartiennent au secret d'Allāh et démontrent le miracle inimitable du Coran, composé des mêmes lettres arabes que celles utilisées par les hommes. Ces versets qui t’ont été révélés sont ceux du Coran et font partie d’un Livre clair qui ne contient aucune ambigüité. Quiconque le médite sait avec certitude qu’il provient d’Allah.","explicationEn":"1. Ta Sin. These are the verses of the Qur’ān and a clear book. The discussion on similar letters has passed in the beginning of Sūrah Al-Baqarah. These verses which are revealed to you are verses of the Qur’ān and a clear book in which there is no confusion. Whoever ponders upon it will know that it is from Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027001","lienPrecedent":"sourate-26-verset-227.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-2.html"},{"numVerset":2,"texteArabe":"هُدًى وَبُشْرَىٰ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"un guide et une bonne annonce aux croyants,","tradEn":"As guidance and good tidings for the believers","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces versets guident et orientent vers la vérité. Ils contiennent aussi une annonce réjouissante adressée à ceux qui croient en Allah et en Ses messagers.","explicationEn":"2. These verses guide to the truth and direct towards it, and give glad-tidings to those who bring faith in Allah and His Messengers.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027002","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-1.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-3.html"},{"numVerset":3,"texteArabe":"الَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ الصَّلَاةَ وَيُؤْتُونَ الزَّكَاةَ وَهُمْ بِالْآخِرَةِ هُمْ يُوقِنُونَ","tradPropre":"qui accomplissent la Salât, acquittent la Zakât et croient avec certitude en l'au-delà.","tradEn":"Who establish prayer and give zakāh, and of the Hereafter they are certain [in faith].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces croyants accomplissent la prière de manière complète et s’acquittent de l’aumône légale en la remettant à qui de droit. De plus, ils sont convaincus que c’est dans l’au-delà que l’on sera récompensé ou puni.","explicationEn":"3. Those who perform prayer in the most complete manner and give Zakat of their wealth by spending it on its recipients, and they are convinced of the reward and punishment in the afterlife.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027003","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-2.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-4.html"},{"numVerset":4,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ الَّذِينَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ بِالْآخِرَةِ زَيَّنَّا لَهُمْ أَعْمَالَهُمْ فَهُمْ يَعْمَهُونَ","tradPropre":"Quant à ceux qui ne croient pas en l'au-delà, Nous embellissons [à leurs yeux] leurs actions, et alors ils deviennent confus et hésitants.","tradEn":"Indeed, for those who do not believe in the Hereafter, We have made pleasing to them their deeds, so they wander blindly.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Aux mécréants qui ne croient pas en l’au-delà et nient la récompense et la rétribution, Nous leur embellissons les mauvaises œuvres et ainsi, ils persistent dans cette voie. Ils sont alors désemparés et incapables de trouver le chemin de la droiture.","explicationEn":"4. The disbelievers who do not bring faith in the afterlife and the reward and punishment therein - I adorned their bad deeds for them so they continued in doing them, thus they are confused without finding their way towards what is right or guidance.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027004","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-3.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-5.html"},{"numVerset":5,"texteArabe":"أُولَائِكَ الَّذِينَ لَهُمْ سُوءُ الْعَذَابِ وَهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ هُمُ الْأَخْسَرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce sont eux qui subiront le pire châtiment, tandis qu'ils seront dans l'au-delà les plus grands perdants.","tradEn":"Those are the ones for whom there will be the worst of punishment, and in the Hereafter they are the greatest losers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce sont ces gens-là qui subiront le pire châtiment dans le bas monde, c’est-à-dire la mort ou la captivité, et ils seront les plus grands perdants dans l’au-delà puisqu’ils entreront, eux et les leurs, en Enfer pour y séjourner éternellement.","explicationEn":"5. Such people will suffer in the worldly life through trials and humiliation and in the Hereafter they suffer the greatest loss, losing themselves and their families on the Day of Judgement and entering Hell forever.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027005","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-4.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-6.html"},{"numVerset":6,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّكَ لَتُلَقَّى الْقُرْآنَ مِنْ لَدُنْ حَكِيمٍ عَلِيمٍ","tradPropre":"Certes, c'est toi qui reçois le Coran, de la part d'un Sage, d'un Savant.","tradEn":"And indeed, [O Muḥammad], you receive the Qur’ān from one Wise and Knowing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ce Coran t’est révélé de la part d’un Dieu Sage dans Sa création, dans Sa gestion ainsi que dans Ses prescriptions et Connaisseur de tout ce qui a trait aux intérêts de Ses serviteurs.","explicationEn":"6. O Messenger, you are receiving this Qur’ān which is being revealed to you from one who is Wise in His creating, managing and legislating, and Knowing, with nothing of the interests of His servants being hidden from Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027006","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-5.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-7.html"},{"numVerset":7,"texteArabe":"إِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِأَهْلِهِ إِنِّي آنَسْتُ نَارًا سَآتِيكُمْ مِنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ أَوْ آتِيكُمْ بِشِهَابٍ قَبَسٍ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُونَ","tradPropre":"(Rappelle) quand Moïse dit à sa famille: «J'ai aperçu un feu; je vais vous en apporter des nouvelles, ou bien je vous apporterai un tison allumé afin que vous vous réchauffiez».","tradEn":"[Mention] when Moses said to his family, \"Indeed, I have perceived a fire. I will bring you from there information or will bring you a burning torch that you may warm yourselves.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi lorsque Moïse dit à sa famille: J’ai vu un feu au loin. Je vais me rendre donc auprès de celui qui l’a allumé afin qu’il nous montre notre chemin, ou pour le moins vous apporter de quoi allumer un feu qui vous réchauffera.","explicationEn":"7. Remember, O Messenger, when Moses said to his family: “I have seen a fire. I shall bring some news from it, from the person who lit it to guide us towards the path, or I shall I bring you a flame of fire taken from it, in the hope that you will light a fire from it to warm yourselves from the cold”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027007","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-6.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-8.html"},{"numVerset":8,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا جَاءَهَا نُودِيَ أَنْ بُورِكَ مَنْ فِي النَّارِ وَمَنْ حَوْلَهَا وَسُبْحَانَ اللَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ","tradPropre":"Lorsqu'il y arriva, on l'appela, - béni soit Celui qui est dans le feu et Celui qui est tout autour, et gloire à Allah, Seigneur des mondes.","tradEn":"But when he came to it, he was called, \"Blessed is whoever is at the fire and whoever is around it. And exalted is Allāh, Lord of the worlds.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque Moïse parvint près du feu, Allah lui dit: Sanctifie Celui qui est dans le feu et les anges qui sont autour de ce feu. Cet ordre visait à ce que Moïse révère le Seigneur des mondes et à ce qu’il exclue de Lui tout attribut qui ne lui sied pas et dont les égarés L’affublaient.","explicationEn":"8. Then when he reached the place of the fire that he saw, Allah called unto him that the one in the fire and the angels surrounding it are blessed.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027008","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-7.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-9.html"},{"numVerset":9,"texteArabe":"يَا مُوسَىٰ إِنَّهُ أَنَا اللَّهُ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ","tradPropre":"«O Moïse, c'est Moi, Allah le Tout Puissant, le Sage».","tradEn":"O Moses, indeed it is I - Allāh, the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis Allah dit: Ô Moïse, c’est Moi Allah, le Puissant à qui personne ne tient tête et le Sage dans Ma création, Ma détermination et Mes prescriptions.","explicationEn":"9. Allah said to him: “O Moses, it is I, Allah, the Mighty whom nobody can overpower, Wise in My creating, managing and legislating.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027009","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-8.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-10.html"},{"numVerset":10,"texteArabe":"وَأَلْقِ عَصَاكَ  فَلَمَّا رَآهَا تَهْتَزُّ كَأَنَّهَا جَانٌّ وَلَّىٰ مُدْبِرًا وَلَمْ يُعَقِّبْ  يَا مُوسَىٰ لَا تَخَفْ إِنِّي لَا يَخَافُ لَدَيَّ الْمُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et: «Jette ton bâton». Quand il le vit remuer comme un serpent, il tourna le dos [pour fuir] sans revenir sur ses pas. «N'aie pas peur, Moïse. Les Messagers n'ont point peur auprès de Moi.","tradEn":"And [he was told], \"Throw down your staff.\" But when he saw it writhing as if it were a snake, he turned in flight and did not return. [Allāh said], \"O Moses, fear not. Indeed, in My presence the messengers do not fear.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Le texte mentionne un type de serpent aux mouvements très rapides.","explicationUnanime":"Ensuite, Allah lui ordonna de jeter son bâton. Moïse obéit et lorsqu’il vit son bâton se mouvoir et se tortiller comme un serpent, il tourna le dos et s’éloigna. Allah lui dit alors: N’aie pas peur de ce serpent car les messagers ne craignent rien auprès de Moi, ni d’un serpent ni d’autre chose.","explicationEn":"10. And throw down your staff”. Moses obeyed. Then when Moses saw it moving and shaking like a snake, he fled turning his back to it and did not return. So Allah said to him: “Do not be scared of it. The Messengers do not fear snakes or anything else in my presence.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027010","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-9.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-11.html"},{"numVerset":11,"texteArabe":"إِلَّا مَنْ ظَلَمَ ثُمَّ بَدَّلَ حُسْنًا بَعْدَ سُوءٍ فَإِنِّي غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Sauf celui qui a commis une injustice puis a remplacé le mal par le bien... alors Je suis Pardonneur et Miséricordieux».","tradEn":"Otherwise, he who wrongs, then substitutes good after evil - indeed, I am Forgiving and Merciful.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Celui qui se montre injuste envers lui-même en commettant un péché puis se repent, Je lui pardonne et lui fais miséricorde.","explicationEn":"11. However, whoever wrongs himself by committing a sin, then repents after that, I am Forgiving to him, Merciful to him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027011","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-10.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-12.html"},{"numVerset":12,"texteArabe":"وَأَدْخِلْ يَدَكَ فِي جَيْبِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَاءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوءٍ  فِي تِسْعِ آيَاتٍ إِلَىٰ فِرْعَوْنَ وَقَوْمِهِ  إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوا قَوْمًا فَاسِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Et introduis ta main dans l'ouverture de ta tunique. Elle sortira blanche et sans aucun mal - un des neuf prodiges à Pharaon et à son peuple, car ils sont vraiment des gens pervers» -.","tradEn":"And put your hand into the opening of your garment [at the breast]; it will come out white without disease. [These are] among the nine signs [you will take] to Pharaoh and his people. Indeed, they have been a people defiantly disobedient.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Introduis ta main dans l’ouverture de ta tunique près de ton cou et tu la ressortiras aussi blanche que la neige sans que tu ne sois atteint de lèpre. Ce sont là deux des neuf signes de ta véracité adressés à Pharaon et à son peuple: la main blanche, le bâton, les années de disette, la pénurie de récoltes, le déluge, l’invasion de sauterelle, l’invasion de poux, l’invasion de grenouilles et le sang.","explicationEn":"12. And put your hand in the opening of your shirt; it will come out after entering it white like snow without being due to leprosy, as part of nine signs which testify to your truthfulness. Along with the hand, they are: the staff, famine, loss of fruits, floods, locusts, lice, frogs, and blood, towards Pharaoh and his people. They were a people left the obedience of Allah by disbelieving in him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027012","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-11.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-13.html"},{"numVerset":13,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا جَاءَتْهُمْ آيَاتُنَا مُبْصِرَةً قَالُوا هَاذَا سِحْرٌ مُبِينٌ","tradPropre":"Et lorsque Nos prodiges leur parvinrent, clairs et explicites, ils dirent: «C'est là une magie évidente!»","tradEn":"But when there came to them Our visible signs, they said, \"This is obvious magic.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque leur parvinrent clairement ces signes par lesquels Nous avons soutenu Moïse, ils dirent: Ce qu’accomplit Moïse est assurément de la magie.","explicationEn":"13. So when these clear and apparent signs of Mine with which I aided Moses came to them, they said: “These signs which Moses has brought are clear magic”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027013","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-12.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-14.html"},{"numVerset":14,"texteArabe":"وَجَحَدُوا بِهَا وَاسْتَيْقَنَتْهَا أَنْفُسُهُمْ ظُلْمًا وَعُلُوًّا  فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُفْسِدِينَ","tradPropre":"Ils les nièrent injustement et orgueilleusement, tandis qu'en eux-mêmes ils y croyaient avec certitude. Regarde donc ce qu'il est advenu des corrupteurs.","tradEn":"And they rejected them, while their [inner] selves were convinced thereof, out of injustice and haughtiness. So see how was the end of the corrupters.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils mécrurent en ces signes manifestes et les rejetèrent bien qu’ils fussent convaincus qu’ils provenaient d’Allah. Leur attitude s’explique par leur injustice et leur arrogance face à la vérité. Vois, ô Messager, quel fut le dénouement que connurent ceux qui ont corrompu la Terre par leur mécréance et leurs actes de désobéissance: Nous les avons tous anéantis et détruits.","explicationEn":"14. They disbelieved in these miracles and did not accept them, despite being convinced they are from Allah, due to their wrongdoing and their arrogance from the truth. So contemplate, O Messenger, how was the outcome of those who cause corruption on earth, due to their disbelief and disobedience; I destroyed them and eradicated all of them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027014","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-13.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-15.html"},{"numVerset":15,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَا دَاوُودَ وَسُلَيْمَانَ عِلْمًا  وَقَالَا الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ الَّذِي فَضَّلَنَا عَلَىٰ كَثِيرٍ مِنْ عِبَادِهِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous avons effectivement donné à David et à Salomon une science; et ils dirent: «Louange à Allah qui nous a favorisés à beaucoup de Ses serviteurs croyants».","tradEn":"And We had certainly given to David and Solomon knowledge, and they said, \"Praise [is due] to Allāh, who has favored us over many of His believing servants.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons donné à David et à son fils Salomon des connaissances, parmi lesquelles la faculté de parler aux oiseaux. David et Salomon exprimèrent leur gratitude à Allah en ces termes: Louange à Allah pour nous avoir favorisés parmi Ses serviteurs croyants par la Prophétie et l’assujettissement des djinns et des démons.","explicationEn":"15. I granted David and his son Solomon knowledge, part of which was the language of birds. David and Solomon said, in gratitude to Allah: “All praise is for Allah who has given us virtue over many of his believing servants, through prophethood and subjugating the jinns”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027015","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-14.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-16.html"},{"numVerset":16,"texteArabe":"وَوَرِثَ سُلَيْمَانُ دَاوُودَ  وَقَالَ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ عُلِّمْنَا مَنْطِقَ الطَّيْرِ وَأُوتِينَا مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ  إِنَّ هَاذَا لَهُوَ الْفَضْلُ الْمُبِينُ","tradPropre":"Et Salomon hérita de David et dit: «O hommes! On nous a appris le langage des oiseaux; et on nous a donné part de toutes choses. C'est là vraiment la grâce évidente.","tradEn":"And Solomon inherited David. He said, \"O people, we have been taught the language of birds, and we have been given from all things. Indeed, this is evident bounty.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon hérita de son père David de la Prophétie, de la science et de la royauté. Il s’adressa en ces termes aux gens en guise de proclamation des bienfaits d’Allah: Ô gens, Allah nous a fait comprendre la langue des oiseaux et nous a accordé tout ce qu’Il accorde habituellement aux prophètes et aux rois. Ceci est assurément une grâce manifeste de Sa part","explicationEn":"16. And Solomon inherited from his father in prophethood, knowledge and kingdom, and he said, relating Allah’s favour on him and his father: “O people, Allah has taught us the language of birds and given us of everything He gave to the prophets and kings. This which He has given us is the clear, apparent grace”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027016","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-15.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-17.html"},{"numVerset":17,"texteArabe":"وَحُشِرَ لِسُلَيْمَانَ جُنُودُهُ مِنَ الْجِنِّ وَالْإِنْسِ وَالطَّيْرِ فَهُمْ يُوزَعُونَ","tradPropre":"Et furent rassemblées pour Salomon, ses armées de djinns, d'hommes et d'oiseaux, et furent placées en rangs.","tradEn":"And gathered for Solomon were his soldiers of the jinn and men and birds, and they were [marching] in rows","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les soldats de Salomon constitués d’humains, de djinns et d’oiseaux furent rassemblés pour que Salomon dispose d'eux et ils se mirent en marche avec discipline.","explicationEn":"17. And for Solomon his armies of men, jinns and birds were gathered, and they were being led orderly.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027017","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-16.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-18.html"},{"numVerset":18,"texteArabe":"حَتَّىٰ إِذَا أَتَوْا عَلَىٰ وَادِ النَّمْلِ قَالَتْ نَمْلَةٌ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّمْلُ ادْخُلُوا مَسَاكِنَكُمْ لَا يَحْطِمَنَّكُمْ سُلَيْمَانُ وَجُنُودُهُ وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Quand ils arrivèrent à la Vallée des Fourmis, une fourmi dit: «O fourmis, entrez dans vos demeures, [de peur] que Salomon et ses armées ne vous écrasent [sous leurs pieds] sans s'en rendre compte».","tradEn":"Until, when they came upon the valley of the ants, an ant said, \"O ants, enter your dwellings that you not be crushed by Solomon and his soldiers while they perceive not.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Arrivés dans la Vallée des Fourmis (nom d’un lieu du Levant), une fourmi dit: Ô ensemble des fourmis, regagnez vos habitations afin que Salomon et ses soldats ne vous écrasent pas sans s’en rendre compte. S’ils s’apercevaient de votre présence, ils ne vous écraseraient certainement pas.","explicationEn":"18. They were being led until when they came to the valley of ants (a place in the Levant), one of the ants said: “O ants, enter your homes so that Solomon and his armies do not destroy you whilst they do not know of you, because if they know of you they will not trample you”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027018","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-17.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-19.html"},{"numVerset":19,"texteArabe":"فَتَبَسَّمَ ضَاحِكًا مِنْ قَوْلِهَا وَقَالَ رَبِّ أَوْزِعْنِي أَنْ أَشْكُرَ نِعْمَتَكَ الَّتِي أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيَّ وَعَلَىٰ وَالِدَيَّ وَأَنْ أَعْمَلَ صَالِحًا تَرْضَاهُ وَأَدْخِلْنِي بِرَحْمَتِكَ فِي عِبَادِكَ الصَّالِحِينَ","tradPropre":"Il sourit, amusé par ses propos et dit: «Permets-moi Seigneur, de rendre grâce pour le bienfait dont Tu m'as comblé ainsi que mes père et mère, et que je fasse une bonne œuvre que tu agrées et fais-moi entrer, par Ta miséricorde, parmi Tes serviteurs vertueux».","tradEn":"So [Solomon] smiled, amused at her speech, and said, \"My Lord, enable me to be grateful for Your favor which You have bestowed upon me and upon my parents and to do righteousness of which You approve. And admit me by Your mercy into [the ranks of] Your righteous servants.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque Salomon entendit les paroles de cette fourmi, il sourit d’amusement et invoqua son Seigneur en ces termes: Ô Seigneur, facilite-moi et inspire-moi de me montrer reconnaissant pour les bienfaits dont Tu m’as comblé et dont Tu as comblé mes parents. Facilite-moi d’œuvrer de manière à mériter Ton agrément et inclus-moi par Ta miséricorde parmi Tes serviteurs vertueux.","explicationEn":"19. When Solomon heard it saying this, he smiled due to this statement of his and he said, calling unto his Lord: “O Lord, enable me and inspire me to be grateful for Your favour which You gave to me and My parents, and enable me to do good actions which please you, and enter me amongst Your righteous servants”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027019","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-18.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-20.html"},{"numVerset":20,"texteArabe":"وَتَفَقَّدَ الطَّيْرَ فَقَالَ مَا لِيَ لَا أَرَى الْهُدْهُدَ أَمْ كَانَ مِنَ الْغَائِبِينَ","tradPropre":"Puis il passa en revue les oiseaux et dit: «Pourquoi ne vois-je pas la huppe? est-elle parmi les absents?","tradEn":"And he took attendance of the birds and said, \"Why do I not see the hoopoe - or is he among the absent?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ensuite, Salomon passa en revue les oiseaux et ne voyant pas la huppe, il dit: Pourquoi ne vois-je pas la huppe? Quelque chose s’interpose-t-il entre elle et moi, m’empêchant ainsi de la voir, ou est-elle absente?","explicationEn":"20. And Solomon took attendance of the birds but did not see the hoopoe, so he said: “What is with me that I do not see the hoopoe? Has something stopped me seeing it or is it from the absentees?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027020","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-19.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-21.html"},{"numVerset":21,"texteArabe":"لَأُعَذِّبَنَّهُ عَذَابًا شَدِيدًا أَوْ لَأَذْبَحَنَّهُ أَوْ لَيَأْتِيَنِّي بِسُلْطَانٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Je la châtierai sévèrement! ou je l'égorgerai! ou bien elle m'apportera un argument explicite».","tradEn":"I will surely punish him with a severe punishment or slaughter him unless he brings me clear authorization.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Après s’être assuré de son absence, il dit: Je la châtierai sévèrement ou l’égorgerai afin de la punir pour son absence, à moins qu’elle ne me présente une excuse justifiée.","explicationEn":"21. He said when its absence became clear to him: “I shall punish it severely, or I shall slaughter it as a punishment for being absent, unless it brings a clear proof to prove its excuse for absence”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027021","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-20.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-22.html"},{"numVerset":22,"texteArabe":"فَمَكَثَ غَيْرَ بَعِيدٍ فَقَالَ أَحَطْتُ بِمَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهِ وَجِئْتُكَ مِنْ سَبَإٍ بِنَبَإٍ يَقِينٍ","tradPropre":"Mais elle n'était restée (absente) que peu de temps et dit: «J'ai appris ce que tu n'as point appris; et je te rapporte de Saba' une nouvelle sûre:","tradEn":"But he [i.e., the hoopoe] stayed not long and said, \"I have encompassed [in knowledge] that which you have not encompassed, and I have come to you from Sheba with certain news.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’absence de la huppe ne dura que peu de temps et lorsqu’elle retourna auprès de Salomon, elle dit: J’ai appris des nouvelles que tu ne connais pas et je t’apporte du pays de Saba une nouvelle véridique et indubitable.","explicationEn":"22. The hoopoe remained absent for a short while. Then when it came, it said to Solomon (peace be upon him): “I discovered what you did not discover, and I have brought to you from Sheba true news in which there is no doubt.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027022","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-21.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-23.html"},{"numVerset":23,"texteArabe":"إِنِّي وَجَدْتُ امْرَأَةً تَمْلِكُهُمْ وَأُوتِيَتْ مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ وَلَهَا عَرْشٌ عَظِيمٌ","tradPropre":"J'ai trouvé qu'une femme est leur reine, que de toute chose elle a été comblée et qu'elle a un trône magnifique.","tradEn":"Indeed, I found [there] a woman ruling them, and she has been given of all things, and she has a great throne.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"J’ai vu qu’il y a à leur tête une femme qui dispose de toutes les prérogatives de la force et de la royauté. J’ai vu aussi qu’elle possède un trône immense à partir duquel elle administre ses sujets.","explicationEn":"23. Indeed, I found [there] a woman ruling them, and she has been given of all things, and she has a great throne. I found a woman who rules them, and this woman has been given of all means of strength and kingdom, and she has a large throne on which she manages the affairs of her people.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027023","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-22.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-24.html"},{"numVerset":24,"texteArabe":"وَجَدْتُهَا وَقَوْمَهَا يَسْجُدُونَ لِلشَّمْسِ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ أَعْمَالَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّبِيلِ فَهُمْ لَا يَهْتَدُونَ","tradPropre":"Je l'ai trouvée, elle et son peuple, se prosternant devant le soleil au lieu d'Allah. Le Diable leur a embelli leurs actions, et les a détournés du droit chemin, et ils ne sont pas bien guidés.","tradEn":"I found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allāh, and Satan has made their deeds pleasing to them and averted them from [His] way, so they are not guided,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"J’ai vu que cette femme et son peuple adorent le soleil au lieu d’adorer Allah. Satan leur a enjolivé leur polythéisme et leurs actes de désobéissance, les détournant ainsi du chemin de la vérité et les rendant incapables de l’emprunter.","explicationEn":"24. I found her and her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allah, and Satan has made their deeds pleasing to them and averted them from [His] way, so they are not guided. I found this woman and I found her people prostrating to the sun instead of Allah, and Satan has beautified for them the actions of idolatry and sins they are on, so he has turned them away from the path of truth, and thus they are not guided to Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027024","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-23.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-25.html"},{"numVerset":25,"texteArabe":"أَلَّا يَسْجُدُوا لِلَّهِ الَّذِي يُخْرِجُ الْخَبْءَ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ وَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُخْفُونَ وَمَا تُعْلِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Que ne se prosternent-ils devant Allah qui fait sortir ce qui est caché dans les cieux et la terre, et qui sait ce que vous cachez et aussi ce que vous divulguez?","tradEn":"[And] so they do not prostrate to Allāh, who brings forth what is hidden within the heavens and the earth and knows what you conceal and what you declare -","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Satan procéda ainsi afin qu’ils ne se prosternent pas devant Allah Seul qui fait tomber la pluie cachée dans le Ciel et pousser les plantes enfouies sous terre. Il est Celui qui est au fait de toutes vos œuvres, que vous les manifestiez ou que vous les dissimuliez, et rien ne Lui en échappe.","explicationEn":"25. [And] so they do not prostrate to Allah, who brings forth what is hidden within the heavens and the earth and knows what you conceal and what you declare. Satan has beautified for them their actions of idolatry and sins, so that they do not prostrate to Allah alone, who brings the rain which He has hidden in the skies and the plants in the earth, and He knows the actions you hide and those you make apparent, none of this being hidden from Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027025","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-24.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-26.html"},{"numVerset":26,"texteArabe":"اللَّهُ لَا إِلَاهَ إِلَّا هُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيمِ ۩","tradPropre":"Allah! Point de divinité à part Lui, le Seigneur du Trône Immense.","tradEn":"Allāh - there is no deity except Him, Lord of the Great Throne.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Sans commune mesure avec le « magnifique trône » de la reine de Saba.","explicationUnanime":"Allah, en dehors de qui il n’existe aucun dieu méritant d’être adoré, le Seigneur du Trône Suprême.","explicationEn":"26. Allah - there is no deity except Him, Lord of the Great Throne. Allah - there is no true god besides, Lord of the Great Throne”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027026","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-25.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-27.html"},{"numVerset":27,"texteArabe":"۞ قَالَ سَنَنْظُرُ أَصَدَقْتَ أَمْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ","tradPropre":"Alors, Salomon dit: «Nous allons voir si tu as dis la vérité ou si tu as menti.","tradEn":"[Solomon] said, \"We will see whether you were truthful or were of the liars.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon répondit à la huppe: Nous vérifierons si tu dis vrai ou si tu mens.","explicationEn":"27. [Solomon] said, \"I will see whether you were truthful or were of the liars. Solomon (peace be upon him) said to the hoopoe: “I shall see if you are truthful in what you claim or were you amongst the liars”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027027","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-26.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-28.html"},{"numVerset":28,"texteArabe":"اذْهَبْ بِكِتَابِي هَاذَا فَأَلْقِهْ إِلَيْهِمْ ثُمَّ تَوَلَّ عَنْهُمْ فَانْظُرْ مَاذَا يَرْجِعُونَ","tradPropre":"Pars avec ma lettre que voici; puis lance-la à eux; ensuite tiens-toi à l'écart d'eux pour voir ce que sera leur réponse.","tradEn":"Take this letter of mine and deliver it to them. Then leave them and see what [answer] they will return.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il écrivit ensuite une lettre et la remit à la huppe en lui disant: Emmène ma missive que voici et lance-la aux gens de Saba. Tiens-toi ensuite à distance d’eux de manière à entendre ce qu’ils diront à son sujet.","explicationEn":"28. Take this letter of mine and deliver it to them. Then leave them and see what [answer] they will return.\" So Solomon wrote a letter and handed it to the hoopoe, and said to it: “Take this letter of mine, and give it to the people of Saba and hand it over to them, and step aside from them so you can hear what they say discuss regarding it”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027028","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-27.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-29.html"},{"numVerset":29,"texteArabe":"قَالَتْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ إِنِّي أُلْقِيَ إِلَيَّ كِتَابٌ كَرِيمٌ","tradPropre":"La reine dit: «O notables! Une noble lettre m'a été lancée.","tradEn":"She said, \"O eminent ones, indeed, to me has been delivered a noble letter.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Après avoir pris connaissance de la missive, la reine dit: Ô notables, une lettre noble et majestueuse m’a été lancée.","explicationEn":"29. She said, \"O eminent ones, indeed, to me has been delivered a noble letter. The queen received the letter and said: “O noble ones, a noble magnificent letter has been given to me.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027029","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-28.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-30.html"},{"numVerset":30,"texteArabe":"إِنَّهُ مِنْ سُلَيْمَانَ وَإِنَّهُ بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيمِ","tradPropre":"Elle vient de Salomon; et c'est: «Au nom d'Allah, le Tout Miséricordieux, le Très Miséricordieux,","tradEn":"Indeed, it is from Solomon, and indeed, it is [i.e., reads]: 'In the name of Allāh, the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful,","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le contenu de cette missive envoyée par Salomon commence par Bismi Llâhi r-Raħmâni r-Raħîmi (Au nom d'Allah, le Tout Miséricordieux, le Très Miséricordieux)","explicationEn":"30. Indeed, it is from Solomon, and Indeed, it reads: 'In the name of Allah, the Gracious, the Merciful. The content of this letter which has been sent by Solomon and which begins with: “In the name of Allah, the Gracious, the Merciful.” is:","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027030","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-29.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-31.html"},{"numVerset":31,"texteArabe":"أَلَّا تَعْلُوا عَلَيَّ وَأْتُونِي مُسْلِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Ne soyez pas hautains avec moi et venez à moi en toute soumission».","tradEn":"Be not haughty with me but come to me in submission [as Muslims].'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon y dit ensuite: Ne soyez pas arrogants et venez à moi en étant soumis au monothéisme auquel je vous invite et en renonçant à votre polythéisme, puisque vous adorez le soleil.","explicationEn":"31. Be not haughty with me but come to me in submission [as Muslims].' \" Do not be arrogant, and come to me obediently and submitting to what I call you towards, namely declaring Allah’s Oneness and leaving associating partners with Him which you are involved in, as you worshipped the sun alongside Him”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027031","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-30.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-32.html"},{"numVerset":32,"texteArabe":"قَالَتْ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ أَفْتُونِي فِي أَمْرِي مَا كُنْتُ قَاطِعَةً أَمْرًا حَتَّىٰ تَشْهَدُونِ","tradPropre":"Elle dit: «O notables! Conseillez-moi sur cette affaire: je ne déciderai rien sans que vous ne soyez présents (pour me conseiller)».","tradEn":"She said, \"O eminent ones, advise me in my affair. I would not decide a matter until you witness [for] me.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis la reine dit: Ô notables et seigneurs, indiquez-moi comment agir dans cette affaire. Je ne prendrai aucune décision sans que vous ne soyez présents et me donniez votre avis.","explicationEn":"32. She said, \"O eminent ones, advise me in my affair. I would not decide a matter until you witness [for] me.\" The queen said: “O noble ones and leaders, explain to me the right course in my matter. I am not going to decide a matter until you come to me and present your opinions regarding it”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027032","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-31.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-33.html"},{"numVerset":33,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا نَحْنُ أُولُو قُوَّةٍ وَأُولُو بَأْسٍ شَدِيدٍ وَالْأَمْرُ إِلَيْكِ فَانْظُرِي مَاذَا تَأْمُرِينَ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Nous sommes détenteurs d'une force et d'une puissance redoutable. Le commandement cependant t'appartient. Regarde donc ce que tu veux ordonner».","tradEn":"They said, \"We are men of strength and of great military might, but the command is yours, so see what you will command.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les notables répondirent: Nous détenons une force immense et notre nuisance est terrible en temps de guerre. Quelle que soit ta décision, elle est la bienvenue car nous disposons des moyens d’exécuter ce que tu nous ordonneras.","explicationEn":"33. They said, \"we are men of strength and of great military might, but the command is yours, so see what you will command.\" The nobles from her people said: “We are people of great power and strong might in warfare, but the opinion is what you think, so see what you will command us to do; we are able to carry it out”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027033","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-32.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-34.html"},{"numVerset":34,"texteArabe":"قَالَتْ إِنَّ الْمُلُوكَ إِذَا دَخَلُوا قَرْيَةً أَفْسَدُوهَا وَجَعَلُوا أَعِزَّةَ أَهْلِهَا أَذِلَّةً  وَكَذَالِكَ يَفْعَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Elle dit: «En vérité, quand les rois entrent dans une cité ils la corrompent, et font de ses honorables citoyens des humiliés. Et c'est ainsi qu'ils agissent.","tradEn":"She said, \"Indeed kings - when they enter a city, they ruin it and render the honored of its people humbled. And thus do they do.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"La reine dit ensuite: Lorsque des rois entrent dans une cité, ils la saccagent, tuent ses habitants et avilissent ses seigneurs et ses notables. C’est ainsi que se comportent toujours les rois lorsqu’ils vainquent les habitants d’une cité afin de les impressionner et de les terrifier.","explicationEn":"34. She said, \"Indeed, kings - when they enter a city, they ruin it and render the honored of its people humbled. And thus do they do. The queen said: “When kings enter any city, they ruin it by the killing, seizing and looting they carry out, and they make its leaders and nobles disgraced, after the honour and protection they enjoyed. And this is how kings always behave when they conquer the people of a city, to plant the seeds of fear and awe in the hearts of the masses.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027034","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-33.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-35.html"},{"numVerset":35,"texteArabe":"وَإِنِّي مُرْسِلَةٌ إِلَيْهِمْ بِهَدِيَّةٍ فَنَاظِرَةٌ بِمَ يَرْجِعُ الْمُرْسَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Moi, je vais leur envoyer un présent, puis je verrai ce que les envoyés ramèneront».","tradEn":"But indeed, I will send to them a gift and see with what [reply] the messengers will return.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Pour ma part, je vais envoyer à l’auteur de la missive et à son peuple un message puis j’attendrai ce que les messagers m’apporteront comme réponse.","explicationEn":"35. But indeed, I will send to them a gift and see with what [reply] the Messengers will return.\" I am sending a gift to the sender of the letter and his people, and I shall see what the messengers bring after sending this gift”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027035","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-34.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-36.html"},{"numVerset":36,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا جَاءَ سُلَيْمَانَ قَالَ أَتُمِدُّونَنِ بِمَالٍ فَمَا آتَانِيَ اللَّهُ خَيْرٌ مِمَّا آتَاكُمْ بَلْ أَنْتُمْ بِهَدِيَّتِكُمْ تَفْرَحُونَ","tradPropre":"Puis, lorsque [la délégation] arriva auprès de Salomon, celui-ci dit: «Est-ce avec des biens que vous voulez m'aider? alors que ce qu'Allah m'a procuré est meilleur que ce qu'Il vous a procuré. Mais c'est vous plutôt qui vous réjouissez de votre cadeau.","tradEn":"So when they came to Solomon, he said, \"Do you provide me with wealth? But what Allāh has given me is better than what He has given you. Rather, it is you who rejoice in your gift.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Puis lorsque le messager de la reine et ses aides chargés du présent de la reine arrivèrent chez Salomon, il réprouva l’initiative de la reine et leur dit: Me donnez-vous ces biens afin que je renonce à vous prêcher? La Prophétie, la royauté et la richesse qu’Allah m’a données valent plus que ce qu’Il vous a donné. C’est vous plutôt qui êtes réjouis des débris de ce monde que l’on vous a concédés.","explicationEn":"36. So when her messenger and his helpers who were with him came carrying the present to Solomon, he criticised them for sending the present, saying: “Are you providing me with wealth to turn me away from you? The prophethood, kingdom and wealth Allah has given me is better than what He has given you. In fact, it is you who are rejoicing on the short-term riches of the world you have been given”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027036","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-35.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-37.html"},{"numVerset":37,"texteArabe":"ارْجِعْ إِلَيْهِمْ فَلَنَأْتِيَنَّهُمْ بِجُنُودٍ لَا قِبَلَ لَهُمْ بِهَا وَلَنُخْرِجَنَّهُمْ مِنْهَا أَذِلَّةً وَهُمْ صَاغِرُونَ","tradPropre":"Retourne vers eux. Nous viendrons avec des armées contre lesquelles ils n'auront aucune résistance, et nous les en expulserons tout humiliés et méprisés.","tradEn":"Return to them, for we will surely come to them with soldiers that they will be powerless to encounter, and we will surely expel them therefrom in humiliation, and they will be debased.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon dit au messager: Retourne auprès des tiens et reprends le présent que tu as apporté. Nous nous rendrons auprès de la reine et de son peuple avec des soldats qu’ils n’auront pas le pouvoir d’affronter. S’ils ne se soumettront pas à moi, nous les expulserons alors de Saba en les humiliant et en les rabaissant après qu’ils eussent été puissants.","explicationEn":"37. Solomon (peace be upon him) said to her messenger: “Return to them with the present you brought, for we will come to her and her people with armies they will not have the power to face, and we will remove them from Sheba disgracefully after the honour they were in, if they do not come to me obediently”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027037","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-36.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-38.html"},{"numVerset":38,"texteArabe":"قَالَ يَا أَيُّهَا الْمَلَأُ أَيُّكُمْ يَأْتِينِي بِعَرْشِهَا قَبْلَ أَنْ يَأْتُونِي مُسْلِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «O notables! Qui de vous m'apportera son trône avant qu'ils ne viennent à moi soumis?»","tradEn":"[Solomon] said, \"O assembly [of jinn], which of you will bring me her throne before they come to me in submission?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon s’adressa ensuite à l’élite rapprochée de son royaume: Ô notables, qui parmi vous m’apportera le trône de la reine avant que son peuple ne vienne à moi soumis?","explicationEn":"38. Solomon (peace be upon him) said, addressing the prominent people of his kingdom: “O eminent ones, which one of you will bring me her royal throne before they come to me obediently?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027038","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-37.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-39.html"},{"numVerset":39,"texteArabe":"قَالَ عِفْرِيتٌ مِنَ الْجِنِّ أَنَا آتِيكَ بِهِ قَبْلَ أَنْ تَقُومَ مِنْ مَقَامِكَ  وَإِنِّي عَلَيْهِ لَقَوِيٌّ أَمِينٌ","tradPropre":"Un djinn redoutable dit: «Je te l'apporterai avant que tu ne te lèves de ta place: pour cela, je suis fort et digne de confiance».","tradEn":"A powerful one from among the jinn said, \"I will bring it to you before you rise from your place, and indeed, I am for this [task] strong and trustworthy.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Un djinn redoutable (‘ifrîtun) lui répondit: Je te l’apporterai bien avant que tu te lèves de la place où tu es. Je dispose de la force nécessaire pour le porter et je suis digne de confiance, puisque je n’en subtiliserai rien.","explicationEn":"39. A rebellious jinn replied saying: “I shall bring her throne to you before you stand from the gathering you are in. I am strong enough to carry it, and can be trusted on what it contains, so I will not take anything of it”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027039","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-38.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-40.html"},{"numVerset":40,"texteArabe":"قَالَ الَّذِي عِنْدَهُ عِلْمٌ مِنَ الْكِتَابِ أَنَا آتِيكَ بِهِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَرْتَدَّ إِلَيْكَ طَرْفُكَ  فَلَمَّا رَآهُ مُسْتَقِرًّا عِنْدَهُ قَالَ هَاذَا مِنْ فَضْلِ رَبِّي لِيَبْلُوَنِي أَأَشْكُرُ أَمْ أَكْفُرُ  وَمَنْ شَكَرَ فَإِنَّمَا يَشْكُرُ لِنَفْسِهِ  وَمَنْ كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ رَبِّي غَنِيٌّ كَرِيمٌ","tradPropre":"Quelqu'un qui avait une connaissance du Livre dit: «Je te l'apporterai avant que tu n'aies cligné de l'œil». Quand ensuite, Salomon a vu le trône installé auprès de lui, il dit: «Cela est de la grâce de mon Seigneur, pour m'éprouver si je suis reconnaissant ou si je suis ingrat. Quiconque est reconnaissant c'est dans son propre intérêt qu'il le fait, et quiconque est ingrat... alors mon Seigneur Se suffit à Lui-même et Il est Généreux».","tradEn":"Said one who had knowledge from the Scripture, \"I will bring it to you before your glance returns to you.\" And when [Solomon] saw it placed before him, he said, \"This is from the favor of my Lord to test me whether I will be grateful or ungrateful. And whoever is grateful - his gratitude is only for [the benefit of] himself. And whoever is ungrateful - then indeed, my Lord is Free of need and Generous.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Un homme vertueux de l’entourage de Salomon, qui était versé dans la science du Livre - science dont fait partie la connaissance du Nom Suprême d'Allah, par lequel lorsqu'on L'invoque il exauce - intervint et dit: Je t’apporterai son trône avant même que tu n’aies cligné de l’œil. J’invoquerai Allah et il apportera le trône. Il invoqua alors Allah et Allah l’exauça. Lorsque Salomon vit le trône devant lui, il dit: Ceci est une faveur de mon Seigneur par laquelle Il me teste: serai-je reconnaissant ou ingrat? Or quiconque est reconnaissant envers Allah est le seul à tirer bénéfice de sa gratitude, puisque la reconnaissance des serviteurs ne profite en rien à Allah. A l’inverse, que celui qui renie les bienfaits d’Allah sache que mon Seigneur se passe de sa gratitude et qu’Il est plein de largesse. L’une des expressions de Sa largesse est qu’Il accorde Ses bienfaits à ceux qui les renient.","explicationEn":"40. A pious knowledgeable man in the presence of Solomon who had knowledge of the scripture, part of which was the greatest name of Allah which Allah accepts prayers when supplicated through, said: “I shall bring her throne to you before your glance returns to you, by praying to Allah to bring it”. So he prayed, and Allah answered his prayer. When Solomon saw her throne placed before him, he said: “This is from the grace of my Lord, to test me whether I am grateful for his favours or ungrateful? Whoever is grateful to Allah, the benefit of his gratefulness will only return to him, because Allah is self sufficient, in no need of anything, is not benefitted or harmed by the gratefulness of His servants. And whoever rejects the favours of Allah and does not thank Him for them, my Lord is self-sufficient, in no need of being shown gratitude, and Generous. Part of His generosity is granting those who deny them”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027040","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-39.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-41.html"},{"numVerset":41,"texteArabe":"قَالَ نَكِّرُوا لَهَا عَرْشَهَا نَنْظُرْ أَتَهْتَدِي أَمْ تَكُونُ مِنَ الَّذِينَ لَا يَهْتَدُونَ","tradPropre":"Et il dit [encore]: «Rendez-lui son trône méconnaissable, nous verrons alors si elle sera guidée ou si elle est du nombre de ceux qui ne sont pas guidés».","tradEn":"He said, \"Disguise for her her throne; we will see whether she will be guided [to truth] or will be of those who is not guided.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Salomon dit: Changez l’apparence de son trône et voyons si elle parvient à le reconnaître ou si elle sera du nombre de ceux qui sont incapables de reconnaître ce qui leur appartient.","explicationEn":"41. Solomon (peace be upon him) said: “Change her royal throne from its original form: we shall see: is she guided to recognising it is her throne or will she be from those who are not guided to recognising their own things?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027041","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-40.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-42.html"},{"numVerset":42,"texteArabe":"فَلَمَّا جَاءَتْ قِيلَ أَهَاكَذَا عَرْشُكِ  قَالَتْ كَأَنَّهُ هُوَ  وَأُوتِينَا الْعِلْمَ مِنْ قَبْلِهَا وَكُنَّا مُسْلِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Quand elle fut venue on lui dit: «Est-ce que ton trône est ainsi?» Elle dit: «C'est comme s'il l'était». - [Salomon dit]: «Le savoir nous a été donné avant elle; et nous étions déjà soumis».","tradEn":"So when she arrived, it was said [to her], \"Is your throne like this?\" She said, \"[It is] as though it was it.\" [Solomon said], \"And we were given knowledge before her, and we have been Muslims [in submission to Allāh].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque la reine de Saba arriva auprès de Salomon, on lui posa la question suivante en guise de test: Ton trône ressemble-t-il à celui-là? Elle répondit: Il se peut que ce soit le mien. Salomon dit alors: Allah nous a fait savoir comment procéder à ce changement d’apparence. Nous Lui sommes soumis et obéissants.","explicationEn":"42. So when the queen of Sheba came to Solomon, it was said to her to test her: “Is this how your throne is?” She answered according to the question: “It is as though it was that”. Allah has granted us knowledge before her and we were submitting to Allah’s order and obeying Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027042","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-41.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-43.html"},{"numVerset":43,"texteArabe":"وَصَدَّهَا مَا كَانَتْ تَعْبُدُ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ  إِنَّهَا كَانَتْ مِنْ قَوْمٍ كَافِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Or, ce qu'elle adorait en dehors d'Allah l'empêchait (d'être croyante) car elle faisait partie d'un peuple mécréant.","tradEn":"And that which she was worshipping other than Allāh had averted her [from submission to Him]. Indeed, she was from a disbelieving people.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Cette reine a été éloignée de l’adoration exclusive d’Allah par les divinités qu’elle adorait par imitation son peuple. Elle appartenait en effet à un peuple de mécréants et était donc à leur image.","explicationEn":"43. And she was turned away from the Oneness of Allah by what she used to worship besides Allah, in following her people and blindly imitating them. She was amongst the people who disbelieve in Allah, so she was a disbeliever like them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027043","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-42.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-44.html"},{"numVerset":44,"texteArabe":"قِيلَ لَهَا ادْخُلِي الصَّرْحَ  فَلَمَّا رَأَتْهُ حَسِبَتْهُ لُجَّةً وَكَشَفَتْ عَنْ سَاقَيْهَا  قَالَ إِنَّهُ صَرْحٌ مُمَرَّدٌ مِنْ قَوَارِيرَ  قَالَتْ رَبِّ إِنِّي ظَلَمْتُ نَفْسِي وَأَسْلَمْتُ مَعَ سُلَيْمَانَ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ","tradPropre":"On lui dit: «Entre dans le palais». Puis, quand elle le vit, elle le prit pour de l'eau profonde et elle se découvrit les jambes. Alors, [Salomon] lui dit: «Ceci est un palais pavé de cristal». - Elle dit: «Seigneur, je me suis fait du tort à moi-même: Je me soumets avec Salomon à Allah, Seigneur des mondes».","tradEn":"She was told, \"Enter the palace.\" But when she saw it, she thought it was a body of water and uncovered her shins [to wade through]. He said, \"Indeed, it is a palace [whose floor is] made smooth with glass.\" She said, \"My Lord, indeed I have wronged myself, and I submit with Solomon to Allāh, Lord of the worlds.\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Sous lequel se trouvait de l’eau. Celui qui n’en était pas informé pensait donc qu’il allait marcher dans l’eau, alors qu’en réalité un plancher de cristal l’en séparait.","explicationUnanime":"On dit à la reine: Entre dans la cour du palais. Elle s’avança et prenant le sol du palais pour de l’eau profonde, elle se découvrit les jambes avant de s’y engager. Salomon lui dit: Ceci est une cour pavée de cristal. Puis il l’invita à l’Islam et la réponse de la reine fut la suivante: Ô Seigneur, j’ai commis une injustice envers moi-même en adorant des divinités avec Toi. Je me soumets maintenant en compagnie de Salomon à Allah, le Seigneur de toutes les créatures.","explicationEn":"44. It was said to her: “Enter the palace” which was like a plane surface. When she entered it, she thought it was water and uncovered her shins to enter it. Solomon (peace be upon him) said: “It is a palace which has been made smooth with glass”. He called her to Islam, so she accepted what he called her towards, saying: “O Lord, I wronged myself by worshipping others besides You, and I have submitted with Solomon to Allah, Lord of all created things”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027044","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-43.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-45.html"},{"numVerset":45,"texteArabe":"وَلَقَدْ أَرْسَلْنَا إِلَىٰ ثَمُودَ أَخَاهُمْ صَالِحًا أَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللَّهَ فَإِذَا هُمْ فَرِيقَانِ يَخْتَصِمُونَ","tradPropre":"Nous envoyâmes effectivement vers les Thamûd leur frère Sâlih. [qui leur dit]: «Adorez Allah». Et voilà qu'ils se divisèrent en deux groupes qui se disputèrent.","tradEn":"And We had certainly sent to Thamūd their brother Ṣāliḥ, [saying], \"Worship Allāh,\" and at once they were two parties conflicting.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Celui des croyants et celui des mécréants.","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons envoyé aux Thamûd leur compatriote Şâlih afin de les appeler à adorer Allah mais ils se divisèrent en deux camps antagonistes, chacun revendiquant détenir la vérité: un camp composé de croyants et un autre composé de mécréants.","explicationEn":"45. And I sent toThamud their brother in lineage Salih (peace be upon him) saying “Worship Allah alone”, but they became two groups after his calling them: a believing group and the other disbelieving, arguing over who is on the truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027045","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-44.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-46.html"},{"numVerset":46,"texteArabe":"قَالَ يَا قَوْمِ لِمَ تَسْتَعْجِلُونَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ قَبْلَ الْحَسَنَةِ  لَوْلَا تَسْتَغْفِرُونَ اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُرْحَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Il dit: «O mon peuple, pourquoi cherchez-vous à hâter le mal plutôt que le bien? Si seulement vous demandiez pardon à Allah? Peut-être vous serait-il fait miséricorde.","tradEn":"He said, \"O my people, why are you impatient for evil before [i.e., instead of] good? Why do you not seek forgiveness of Allāh that you may receive mercy?\"","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> L’impiété plutôt que la foi. Autre sens : pourquoi vous hâtez-vous d’appeler le châtiment d’Allah sur vous plutôt que Sa miséricorde ?","explicationUnanime":"Şâliħ leur dit: Pourquoi recherchez-vous à hâter le châtiment plutôt que la miséricorde? Et si au lieu de cela vous demandiez à Allah de pardonner vos péchés, peut-être vous ferait-Il miséricorde?","explicationEn":"46. Salih (peace be upon him) said: “why do you seek to hasten the punishment instead of seeking Allah's mercy? Why do you not seek forgiveness from Allah for your sins, in the hope that he will forgive you?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027046","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-45.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-47.html"},{"numVerset":47,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا اطَّيَّرْنَا بِكَ وَبِمَنْ مَعَكَ  قَالَ طَائِرُكُمْ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ  بَلْ أَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تُفْتَنُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Nous voyons en toi et en ceux qui sont avec toi, des porteurs de malheur». Il dit: «Votre sort dépend d'Allah. Mais vous êtes plutôt des gens qu'on soumet à la tentation.","tradEn":"They said, \"We consider you a bad omen, you and those with you.\" He said, \"Your omen [i.e., fate] is with Allāh. Rather, you are a people being tested.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les siens, obstinés à rejeter la vérité, lui répondirent: Nous considérons que toi et les croyants qui t’accompagnent, portez malheur. Şâliħ leur rétorqua: Le malheur que vous prévoyez n’est connu que d’Allah et rien ne Lui en échappe. Vous êtes plutôt des gens que l’on teste par le bien qui vous est accordé et par le mal qui vous atteint.","explicationEn":"47. His people said to him, in stubbornness from the truth: “I consider you and the believers with you a bad omen”. Salih (peace be upon him) said: “The birds that you drive away due to the difficulties that which has afflicted you from what you dislike and you attribute as a bad omen is actually decreed from Allah and He has knowledge of that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027047","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-46.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-48.html"},{"numVerset":48,"texteArabe":"وَكَانَ فِي الْمَدِينَةِ تِسْعَةُ رَهْطٍ يُفْسِدُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَا يُصْلِحُونَ","tradPropre":"Et il y avait dans la ville un groupe de neuf individus qui semaient le désordre sur terre et ne faisaient rien de bon.","tradEn":"And there were in the city nine family heads causing corruption in the land and not amending [its affairs].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dans la ville d’Al-Ħijr, il y avait neuf hommes qui, par leur mécréance et leurs actes de désobéissance, semaient le désordre sur Terre et s’abstenaient d’avoir la foi et d’accomplir de bonnes œuvres.","explicationEn":"48. And in the city of Hijr there were nine men who would cause corruption on earth through disbelief and sins, and they would not reform in it through faith and good actions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027048","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-47.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-49.html"},{"numVerset":49,"texteArabe":"قَالُوا تَقَاسَمُوا بِاللَّهِ لَنُبَيِّتَنَّهُ وَأَهْلَهُ ثُمَّ لَنَقُولَنَّ لِوَلِيِّهِ مَا شَهِدْنَا مَهْلِكَ أَهْلِهِ وَإِنَّا لَصَادِقُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils dirent: «Jurons par Allah que nous l'attaquerons de nuit, lui et sa famille. Ensuite nous dirons à celui qui est chargé de le venger: «Nous n'avons pas assisté à l'assassinat de sa famille, et nous sommes sincères».","tradEn":"They said, \"Take a mutual oath by Allāh that we will kill him by night, he and his family. Then we will say to his executor, 'We did not witness the destruction of his family, and indeed, we are truthful.'\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"L’un d’eux dit aux autres: Que chacun de nous prête serment par Allah de nous rendre chez Şâliħ de nuit et de le tuer lui et sa famille. Nous dirons ensuite à celui de ses proches chargé de réclamer que vengeance que nous n’avons pas participé au crime et que nous disons la vérité.","explicationEn":"49. They said to one another: “Each one of you should swear by Allah that we will go to him and the believers with him at night, then we will kill them and then say to the one responsible for avenging his blood: ‘We were not present at the murder of Salih or the murder of his followers, and we are truthful in what we have said’”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027049","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-48.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-50.html"},{"numVerset":50,"texteArabe":"وَمَكَرُوا مَكْرًا وَمَكَرْنَا مَكْرًا وَهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Ils ourdirent une ruse et Nous ourdîmes une ruse sans qu'ils s'en rendent compte.","tradEn":"And they planned a plan, and We planned a plan, while they perceived not.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ils mirent au point un stratagème secret afin d’exterminer Şâliħ et ses disciples croyants. Or Nous mîmes également au point un stratagème afin de secourir Şâliħ, le sauver de leur conspiration et anéantir les mécréants de son peuple, mais ils n’en étaient pas conscients.","explicationEn":"50. And they secretly made a plan to destroy Salih and his followers amongst the believers, and I also made a plan to help him, save him from their plan and to destroy the disbelievers from his people, whilst they did not know that.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027050","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-49.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-51.html"},{"numVerset":51,"texteArabe":"فَانْظُرْ كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ مَكْرِهِمْ أَنَّا دَمَّرْنَاهُمْ وَقَوْمَهُمْ أَجْمَعِينَ","tradPropre":"Regarde donc ce qu'a été la conséquence de leur stratagème: Nous les fîmes périr, eux et tout leur peuple.","tradEn":"Then look how was the outcome of their plan - that We destroyed them and their people, all.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, vois donc ce qu’il est advenu de leur stratagème et de leur conspiration. Nous avons abattu sur eux un châtiment qui les a exterminés jusqu’au dernier","explicationEn":"51. So contemplate, O Messenger, what was the outcome and end of their planning and scheming; did they achieve what they were intending? No. In fact, I totally uprooted them with a punishment from Myself so they were all destroyed.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027051","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-50.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-52.html"},{"numVerset":52,"texteArabe":"فَتِلْكَ بُيُوتُهُمْ خَاوِيَةً بِمَا ظَلَمُوا  إِنَّ فِي ذَالِكَ لَآيَةً لِقَوْمٍ يَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Voilà donc leurs maisons désertes à cause de leurs méfaits. C'est bien là un avertissement pour des gens qui savent.","tradEn":"So those are their houses, desolate because of the wrong they had done. Indeed in that is a sign for people who know.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Voici leurs maisons, dont les toits et les murs se sont effondrés, vides de leurs habitants en raison de l’injustice de ces derniers. Le châtiment qu’ils ont subi pour leur injustice est une leçon adressée aux croyants puisque ce sont eux qui méditent les signes.","explicationEn":"52. So those are their homes whose walls have fallen on their roofs, and they have remained empty of inhabitants, due to their wrongdoing. In the punishment which has afflicted them due to their wrongdoing is a lesson for people who believe, as they are the ones who take lessons from the signs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027052","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-51.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-53.html"},{"numVerset":53,"texteArabe":"وَأَنْجَيْنَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَكَانُوا يَتَّقُونَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous sauvâmes ceux qui avaient cru et étaient pieux.","tradEn":"And We saved those who believed and used to fear Allāh.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous avons sauvé ceux parmi le peuple de Şâliħ qui croyaient en Allah, se conformaient à Ses commandements et renonçaient à Ses interdits.","explicationEn":"53. And I saved those who believed from the people of Salih (peace be upon him), and they used to be mindful of Allah by carrying out His orders and refraining from His prohibitions.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027053","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-52.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-54.html"},{"numVerset":54,"texteArabe":"وَلُوطًا إِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ أَتَأْتُونَ الْفَاحِشَةَ وَأَنْتُمْ تُبْصِرُونَ","tradPropre":"[Et rappelle-leur] Lot, quand il dit à son peuple: «Vous livrez-vous à la turpitude [l'homosexualité] alors que vous voyez clair».","tradEn":"And [mention] Lot, when he said to his people, \"Do you commit immorality while you are seeing?","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Ou : alors que vous en connaissez la gravité.","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi lorsque Loth réprimanda les siens en leur disant: Vous adonnez-vous à cette pratique abominable qu’est la sodomie, publiquement dans vos assemblées et à la vue de tous?","explicationEn":"54. O Messenger, remember Lot when he said to his people, reprimanding them and criticising them: “Do you come to the indecent act, which is sodomy in your meetings, openly watching one another?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027054","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-53.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-55.html"},{"numVerset":55,"texteArabe":"أَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَأْتُونَ الرِّجَالَ شَهْوَةً مِنْ دُونِ النِّسَاءِ  بَلْ أَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تَجْهَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Vous allez aux hommes au lieu de femmes pour assouvir vos désirs? Vous êtes plutôt un peuple ignorant.","tradEn":"Do you indeed approach men with desire instead of women? Rather, you are a people behaving ignorantly.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Préférez-vous avoir des rapports charnels avec des hommes plutôt qu’avec des femmes, n’ayant pas pour finalité de cet acte de parvenir au contentement charnel ou d’avoir une progéniture mais par simple pulsion bestiale? Vous êtes certainement des gens qui ignorent qu’il leur est obligatoire d’avoir la foi, d’être purs et de ne pas désobéir à Allah.","explicationEn":"55. Do you come to men lustfully, leaving the women, not intending chastity or children but only to fulfil animalistic lust? But rather you are a people ignorant of what is necessary upon you, namely faith, purity and staying far from sins”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027055","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-54.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-56.html"},{"numVerset":56,"texteArabe":"۞ فَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهِ إِلَّا أَنْ قَالُوا أَخْرِجُوا آلَ لُوطٍ مِنْ قَرْيَتِكُمْ  إِنَّهُمْ أُنَاسٌ يَتَطَهَّرُونَ","tradPropre":"Puis son peuple n'eut que cette réponse: «Expulsez de votre cité la famille de Lot! Car ce sont des gens qui affectent la pureté.","tradEn":"But the answer of his people was not except that they said, \"Expel the family of Lot from your city. Indeed, they are people who keep themselves pure.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il n’obtint d’eux comme réponse, que celle-ci: Expulsez la famille de Loth de votre cité puisqu’ils prétendent refuser les souillures et les impuretés. Ces paroles visaient à tourner en dérision les proches de Loth qui ne prenaient pas part à leurs pratiques et les réprouvaient.","explicationEn":"56. But his people did not have an answer besides their saying: “Remove the family of Lot from your city. They are a people who want to stay pure from dirt and impurity”. They said this to mock the family of Lot who would not join them in the immoral acts they used to commit, but rather they would condemn them for committing them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027056","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-55.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-57.html"},{"numVerset":57,"texteArabe":"فَأَنْجَيْنَاهُ وَأَهْلَهُ إِلَّا امْرَأَتَهُ قَدَّرْنَاهَا مِنَ الْغَابِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Nous le sauvâmes ainsi que sa famille, sauf sa femme pour qui Nous avions déterminé qu'elle serait du nombre des exterminés.","tradEn":"So We saved him and his family, except for his wife; We destined her to be of those who remained behind.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous sauvâmes donc Loth ainsi que sa famille, excepté son épouse que Nous avons condamnée à subir le châtiment et à être du nombre des anéantis.","explicationEn":"57. So we saved him and his family, except for his wife, who was decreed to be from those who remained behind for the punishment, so she may be from those who were destroyed.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027057","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-56.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-58.html"},{"numVerset":58,"texteArabe":"وَأَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ مَطَرًا  فَسَاءَ مَطَرُ الْمُنْذَرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et Nous fîmes pleuvoir sur eux une pluie (de pierres). Et quelle mauvaise pluie que celle des gens prévenus!","tradEn":"And We rained upon them a rain [of stones], and evil was the rain of those who were warned.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Nous fîmes pleuvoir sur eux du Ciel une pluie de pierres et ce fut une pluie de malheur qui extermina ceux qu'on a menacés de châtiment et qui ont fait fi de cette menace.","explicationEn":"58. And I rained stones of baked clay on the people of Lot. Dreadful is the rain of those who have been warned such as the people of Lot who did not respond to him, and in fact remained on their disbelief, misguidance and committing immorality.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027058","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-57.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-59.html"},{"numVerset":59,"texteArabe":"قُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ وَسَلَامٌ عَلَىٰ عِبَادِهِ الَّذِينَ اصْطَفَىٰ  آللَّهُ خَيْرٌ أَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Louange à Allah et paix sur Ses serviteurs qu'Il a élus!» Lequel est meilleur: Allah ou bien ce qu'ils Lui associent?","tradEn":"Say, [O Muḥammad], \"Praise be to Allāh, and peace upon His servants whom He has chosen. Is Allāh better or what they associate with Him?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis: Louange à Allah pour Ses bienfaits et qu’Il sauve les Compagnons du Prophète du châtiment qu’Il infligea au peuple de Loth. Est-ce Allah, le Dieu méritant d’être adoré et Celui qui possède toute chose, qui est meilleur ou bien les divinités inutiles et inoffensives que les polythéistes adorent?","explicationEn":"59. O Messenger, say: “All praise is for Allah for his favours, and peace from him on His Messengers whom He chose to convey His religion”. Is Allah, the true god in whose Hand is the kingdom of everything, better or the gods which the idolaters worship, which do not possess benefit or harm?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027059","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-58.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-60.html"},{"numVerset":60,"texteArabe":"أَمَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضَ وَأَنْزَلَ لَكُمْ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ مَاءً فَأَنْبَتْنَا بِهِ حَدَائِقَ ذَاتَ بَهْجَةٍ مَا كَانَ لَكُمْ أَنْ تُنْبِتُوا شَجَرَهَا  أَإِلَاهٌ مَعَ اللَّهِ  بَلْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ يَعْدِلُونَ","tradPropre":"N'est-ce pas Lui qui a créé les cieux et la terre et qui vous a fait descendre du ciel une eau avec laquelle Nous avons fait pousser des jardins pleins de beauté. Vous n'étiez nullement capables de faire pousser leurs arbres. Y a-t-il donc une divinité avec Allah? Non, mais ce sont des gens qui Lui donnent des égaux.","tradEn":"[More precisely], is He [not best] who created the heavens and the earth and sent down for you rain from the sky, causing to grow thereby gardens of joyful beauty which you could not [otherwise] have grown the trees thereof? Is there a deity with Allāh? [No], but they are a people who ascribe equals [to Him].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"N’est-Il pas Celui qui a créé les Cieux et la Terre sans modèle préalable et a fait descendre sur vous du Ciel l’eau de la pluie, ô gens? Nous avons ensuite fait pousser pour vous, grâce à cette eau des vergers splendides? Vous n’auriez jamais été capables de faire pousser les arbres de ces vergers et c’est Allah qui s’en est chargé. Y a-t-il un autre Dieu qui accomplit cela de concert avec Allah? Non, mais ce sont des gens qui dévient de la vérité et mettent injustement sur un même pied d’égalité le Créateur et les créatures.","explicationEn":"60. Is He not best who created the heavens and the earth without any precedent, and He sent down for you, O people, rainwater from the sky, then He grew for you gardens of beauty? It was not for you to grow the trees of these gardens, due to your being unable to do that. So it is Allah who grew them. Is there any true god alongside Allah? No, but rather they are a people who turn away from the truth, so they unjustly make the creation equal with the Creator.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027060","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-59.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-61.html"},{"numVerset":61,"texteArabe":"أَمَّنْ جَعَلَ الْأَرْضَ قَرَارًا وَجَعَلَ خِلَالَهَا أَنْهَارًا وَجَعَلَ لَهَا رَوَاسِيَ وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ حَاجِزًا  أَإِلَاهٌ مَعَ اللَّهِ  بَلْ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ","tradPropre":"N'est-ce pas Lui qui a établi la terre comme lieu de séjour, placé des rivières à travers elle, lui a assigné des montagnes fermes et établi une séparation entre les deux mers, - Y a-t-il donc une divinité avec Allah? Non, mais la plupart d'entre eux ne savent pas.","tradEn":"Is He [not best] who made the earth a stable ground and placed within it rivers and made for it firmly set mountains and placed between the two seas a barrier? Is there a deity with Allāh? [No], but most of them do not know.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"N’est-Il pas Celui qui fit en sorte que la Terre soit stable et ferme et qu’elle ne tremble pas sous ses habitants? N’est-Il pas Celui qui y a fait couler des rivières et y a placé des montagnes bien ancrées? N’est-Il pas Celui qui a établi une séparation entre l’eau douce et l’eau salée qui empêche leur mélange et que l’eau douce potable ne soit rendue imbuvable par le sel? Y a-t-il un autre Dieu qui accomplit cela de concert avec Allah? Non, mais la plupart ne savent pas cela car s’ils le savaient, ils n’auraient associé à Allah aucune de Ses créatures.","explicationEn":"61. Is He not best who made the earth firm and still, without it shaking those on it, and made within it rivers that flow, and made for it firm mountains, and made between two seas, salty and sweet, a barrier which stops the salty mixing with the sweet so that it does not spoil it and then making it unsuitable for drinking? Is there a true god alongside Allah who can make all that happen? No, but most of them do not know. Had they known, they would not have associated any of Allah’s creation with Him as a partner.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027061","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-60.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-62.html"},{"numVerset":62,"texteArabe":"أَمَّنْ يُجِيبُ الْمُضْطَرَّ إِذَا دَعَاهُ وَيَكْشِفُ السُّوءَ وَيَجْعَلُكُمْ خُلَفَاءَ الْأَرْضِ  أَإِلَاهٌ مَعَ اللَّهِ  قَلِيلًا مَا تَذَكَّرُونَ","tradPropre":"N'est-ce pas Lui qui répond à l'angoissé quand il L'invoque, et qui enlève le mal, et qui vous fait succéder sur la terre, génération après génération, - Y a-t-il donc une divinité avec Allah? C'est rare que vous vous rappeliez!","tradEn":"Is He [not best] who responds to the desperate one when he calls upon Him and removes evil and makes you inheritors of the earth? Is there a deity with Allāh? Little do you remember.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"N’est-Il pas Celui qui exauce quiconque L'invoque lorsqu’il se retrouve dans la gêne et le malheur? N’est-Il pas Celui qui fait disparaître les maux de la maladie, de la pauvreté et autres qui atteignent l’être humain et fait de vous les successeurs de ceux qui vous précèdent génération après génération? Y a-t-il un autre Dieu qui accomplit cela de concert avec Allah? Non, mais il est rare que vous déduisiez des enseignements de cela.","explicationEn":"62. Is He not best who responds to the call of the distressed when he calls upon Him, seeking for his harm to be removed, and who removes what the human finds bad such as illness and poverty, and who makes you deputies on earth, succeeding one another generation after generation? Is there a true god alongside Allah who makes all that happen? No. Little do you take heed and consider.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027062","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-61.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-63.html"},{"numVerset":63,"texteArabe":"أَمَّنْ يَهْدِيكُمْ فِي ظُلُمَاتِ الْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ وَمَنْ يُرْسِلُ الرِّيَاحَ بُشْرًا بَيْنَ يَدَيْ رَحْمَتِهِ  أَإِلَاهٌ مَعَ اللَّهِ  تَعَالَى اللَّهُ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُونَ","tradPropre":"N'est-ce pas Lui qui vous guide dans les ténèbres de la terre et de la mer, et qui envoie les vents, comme une bonne annonce précédent Sa grâce. - Y a-t-il donc une divinité avec Allah? Allah est Très Elevé au-dessus de ce qu'ils [Lui] associent.","tradEn":"Is He [not best] who guides you through the darknesses of the land and sea and who sends the winds as good tidings before His mercy? Is there a deity with Allāh? High is Allāh above whatever they associate with Him.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"N’est-Il pas Celui qui vous guide dans les ténèbres de la terre ferme et de la mer grâce aux repères et aux astres qu’Il a créés à votre attention? N’est-Il pas Celui qui envoie les vents en guise d’annonce de l’imminence de la pluie par laquelle Il fait miséricorde à Ses serviteurs? Y a-t-il un autre Dieu qui accomplit cela de concert avec Allah? Qu’Allah soit sanctifié et élevé au-dessus de ce qu’ils Lui associent comme créatures.","explicationEn":"63. Is He not best who guides you in the darkness of the land and the darkness of the sea through the signs and stars He fixes for you, and who sends winds to give good news of close rainfall through which He will have mercy on His servants? Is there a true god alongside Allah who makes all that happen and decrees it? Allah is purified and far removed from the partners the creation associate with Him","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027063","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-62.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-64.html"},{"numVerset":64,"texteArabe":"أَمَّنْ يَبْدَأُ الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيدُهُ وَمَنْ يَرْزُقُكُمْ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ وَالْأَرْضِ  أَإِلَاهٌ مَعَ اللَّهِ  قُلْ هَاتُوا بُرْهَانَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صَادِقِينَ","tradPropre":"N'est-ce pas Lui qui commence la création, puis la refait, et qui vous nourrit du ciel et de la terre. Y a-t-il donc une divinité avec Allah? Dis: «Apportez votre preuve, si vous êtes véridiques!»","tradEn":"Is He [not best] who begins creation and then repeats it and who provides for you from the heaven and earth? Is there a deity with Allāh? Say, \"Produce your proof, if you should be truthful.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"N’est-Il pas Celui qui commence la création du fœtus dans l’utérus et la poursuit étape par étape, puis fait vivre ce fœtus après qu’il ait été un corps inerte? N’est-Il pas Celui qui vous pourvoit lorsqu’il fait descendre la pluie du Ciel sur vous et lorsqu’Il fait pousser pour vous les plantes de sous terre? Y a-t-il un autre Dieu qui accomplit cela de concert avec Allah? Ô Messager, dis à ces polythéistes: Apportez les arguments qui plaident en faveur de votre polythéisme si vous êtes véridiques lorsque vous prétendez être dans le vrai.","explicationEn":"64. Is He not best who begins the creation in the wombs, stage after stage, then He will restore it after He gives it death, and who provides you from the sky with water that descends from its direction, and who provides you from the earth with plants He makes grow therein? Is there a true god alongside Allah who makes all that happen and decrees it? Say - O Messenger, to these idolaters: “Bring your proofs for the idolatry you are on, if you are true in your claim that you are on the truth”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027064","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-63.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-65.html"},{"numVerset":65,"texteArabe":"قُلْ لَا يَعْلَمُ مَنْ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَالْأَرْضِ الْغَيْبَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ  وَمَا يَشْعُرُونَ أَيَّانَ يُبْعَثُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Nul de ceux qui sont dans les cieux et sur la terre ne connaît l'Inconnaissable, à part Allah». Et ils ne savent pas quand ils seront ressuscités!","tradEn":"Say, \"None in the heavens and earth knows the unseen except Allāh, and they do not perceive when they will be resurrected.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis: Personne parmi les anges du Ciel et les habitants de la Terre ne connaît l’Invisible. Seul Allah le connaît. De même, aucun de ceux qui peuplent le Ciel et la Terre ne savent quand ils seront ressuscités afin d’être rétribués et Seul Allah le sait.","explicationEn":"65. O Messenger, say: The Ghaib is not known by the angels in the heavens or the people on earth. However Allah alone is the one who knows it. And nobody in the heavens or the earth knows when they will be raised for recompense besides Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027065","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-64.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-66.html"},{"numVerset":66,"texteArabe":"بَلِ ادَّارَكَ عِلْمُهُمْ فِي الْآخِرَةِ  بَلْ هُمْ فِي شَكٍّ مِنْهَا  بَلْ هُمْ مِنْهَا عَمُونَ","tradPropre":"Mais leurs sciences se sont rejointes au sujet de l'autre monde. Ils doutent plutôt là-dessus. Ou plutôt ils sont aveugles à son sujet.","tradEn":"Rather, their knowledge is arrested concerning the Hereafter. Rather, they are in doubt about it. Rather, they are, concerning it, blind.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Autre sens : mais ils en seront pleinement informés dans l’au-delà, tandis qu’aujourd’hui ils doutent de sa réalité, aveugles aux preuves qui leur sont apportées.","explicationUnanime":"Leurs connaissances de l’au-delà sont-elles devenues telles qu’ils sont certains de ce qu’il adviendra d’eux dans l’autre monde? Ils sont plutôt emplis de doutes à ce sujet au point d’être semblables à des aveugles.","explicationEn":"66. But rather their knowledge in the afterlife will become complete, due to their seeing it with their own eyes after the Messengers used to inform them of it when it was unseen, but they used to deny it because they had not seen it. And they were in doubt and confusion regarding the afterlife in their worldly life, for their eyes and hearts had become blind towards it.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027066","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-65.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-67.html"},{"numVerset":67,"texteArabe":"وَقَالَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا أَإِذَا كُنَّا تُرَابًا وَآبَاؤُنَا أَئِنَّا لَمُخْرَجُونَ","tradPropre":"Et ceux qui ne croient pas disent: «Est-ce que, quand nous serons poussière, nous et nos pères, est-ce que vraiment on nous fera sortir (de nos tombes)?","tradEn":"And those who disbelieve say, \"When we have become dust as well as our forefathers, will we indeed be brought out [of the graves]?","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ceux qui mécroient disent sur un ton dubitatif: Est-il possible que nous soyons ressuscités après que nous soyons morts et devenus poussière?","explicationEn":"67. Those who disbelieved said denyingly: “When we die and become dust, is it possible we will be raised alive?","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027067","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-66.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-68.html"},{"numVerset":68,"texteArabe":"لَقَدْ وُعِدْنَا هَاذَا نَحْنُ وَآبَاؤُنَا مِنْ قَبْلُ إِنْ هَاذَا إِلَّا أَسَاطِيرُ الْأَوَّلِينَ","tradPropre":"Certes, on nous l'a promis à nous et à nos pères, auparavant. Ce ne sont que des contes d'anciens!»","tradEn":"We have been promised this, we and our forefathers, before. This is not but legends of the former peoples.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On nous a déjà promis d’être tous ressuscités et on a également promis cela à nos ancêtres auparavant. Seulement, nous n’avons pas vu cette promesse se réaliser. Ce ne sont donc que des mensonges consignés par les anciens dans leurs livres.","explicationEn":"68. We were promised and our fathers were promised before that we will all be raised, but we have not seen that promise come true. This promise we were all made is nothing but lies of the former people who recorded them in their books”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027068","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-67.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-69.html"},{"numVerset":69,"texteArabe":"قُلْ سِيرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوا كَيْفَ كَانَ عَاقِبَةُ الْمُجْرِمِينَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Parcourez la terre et voyez ce qu'il est advenu des criminels».","tradEn":"Say, [O Muḥammad], \"Proceed [i.e., travel] through the land and observe how was the end of the criminals.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis à ces gens qui rejettent la réalité de la Ressuscitation: Parcourez n’importe quelle contrée sur Terre et méditez la fin des criminels qui rejetaient la réalité de la Ressuscitation: Nous les avons anéantis pour leur rejet.","explicationEn":"69. O Messenger! Say to these deniers of the resurrection: “Travel in any direction on earth, then ponder over what was the outcome of the evildoers who denied the resurrection; I destroyed them due to their denying it”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027069","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-68.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-70.html"},{"numVerset":70,"texteArabe":"وَلَا تَحْزَنْ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا تَكُنْ فِي ضَيْقٍ مِمَّا يَمْكُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Et ne t'afflige pas sur eux et ne sois pas angoissé à cause de leur complot.","tradEn":"And grieve not over them or be in distress from what they conspire.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ne t’attriste pas du refus des polythéistes de répondre favorablement à ta prédication et ne te tourmente pas pour leur complot car Allah te secourra contre eux.","explicationEn":"70. Do not grieve due to the idolaters turning away from your call nor should your bosom become tight or should you worry due to their scheming against you, for Allah is with you and He will help you against them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027070","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-69.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-71.html"},{"numVerset":71,"texteArabe":"وَيَقُولُونَ مَتَىٰ هَاذَا الْوَعْدُ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صَادِقِينَ","tradPropre":"Et ils disent: «Pour quand cette promesse si vous êtes véridiques?»","tradEn":"And they say, \"When is [the fulfillment of] this promise, if you should be truthful?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Les mécréants de ton peuple qui rejettent la Ressuscitation disent: Quand donc s’abattra sur nous le châtiment que toi et les croyants nous promettez, si vous êtes véridiques dans ce que vous prétendez?","explicationEn":"71. The disbelievers amongst your people who deny the resurrection say: “When will the punishment you and the believers promise us occur, if you are true in what you claim of that?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027071","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-70.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-72.html"},{"numVerset":72,"texteArabe":"قُلْ عَسَىٰ أَنْ يَكُونَ رَدِفَ لَكُمْ بَعْضُ الَّذِي تَسْتَعْجِلُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Il se peut qu'une partie de ce que vous cherchez à hâter soit déjà sur vos talons».","tradEn":"Say, \"Perhaps it is close behind you [i.e., very near] - some of that for which you are impatient.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis-leur: Il se peut qu’une part du châtiment que vous cherchez à hâter s’abatte sur vous sous peu.","explicationEn":"72. O Messenger, say to them: “Perhaps some of the punishment you are hastily seeking has already come near”.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027072","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-71.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-73.html"},{"numVerset":73,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَلَاكِنَّ أَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَشْكُرُونَ","tradPropre":"Certes, ton Seigneur est pourvoyeur de grâce aux hommes, mais la plupart d'entre eux ne sont pas reconnaissants.","tradEn":"And indeed, your Lord is the possessor of bounty for the people, but most of them are not grateful.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ton Seigneur comble les gens de Sa grâce lorsqu’Il ne s’empresse pas de les châtier malgré leur mécréance et leur désobéissance. Or la plupart d’entre eux ne Lui sont pas reconnaissants pour les bienfaits dont Il les comble.","explicationEn":"73. And your Lord, O Messenger, is graceful towards the people, as He is leaving punishing them quickly despite the disbelief and sins they are upon. However, most people do not thank Allah for the favours He gives them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027073","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-72.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-74.html"},{"numVerset":74,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَيَعْلَمُ مَا تُكِنُّ صُدُورُهُمْ وَمَا يُعْلِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Certes, ton Seigneur sait ce que cachent leurs poitrines et ce qu'ils divulguent.","tradEn":"And indeed, your Lord knows what their breasts conceal and what they declare.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ton Seigneur sait ce que dissimulent les cœurs de Ses serviteurs et sait ce qu’ils manifestent. Rien ne Lui échappe de tout cela et Il les rétribuera en conséquence.","explicationEn":"74. And your Lord knows what the hearts of His servants hide and what they make apparent. None of that is hidden from Him.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027074","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-73.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-75.html"},{"numVerset":75,"texteArabe":"وَمَا مِنْ غَائِبَةٍ فِي السَّمَاءِ وَالْأَرْضِ إِلَّا فِي كِتَابٍ مُبِينٍ","tradPropre":"Et il n'y a rien de caché, dans le ciel et la terre, qui ne soit dans un Livre explicite.","tradEn":"And there is nothing concealed within the heaven and the earth except that it is in a clear Register.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il n’existe pas de chose, dans le Ciel ou sur Terre, inconnue des gens, qui ne soit consignée dans un Livre explicite qui est la Table Préservée.","explicationEn":"75. And there is nothing hidden from the people in the sky nor anything hidden from them on earth except that it is in a clear book, which is the Preserved Tablet.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027075","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-74.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-76.html"},{"numVerset":76,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ هَاذَا الْقُرْآنَ يَقُصُّ عَلَىٰ بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ أَكْثَرَ الَّذِي هُمْ فِيهِ يَخْتَلِفُونَ","tradPropre":"Ce Coran raconte aux Enfants d'Israël la plupart des sujets sur lesquels ils divergent,","tradEn":"Indeed, this Qur’ān relates to the Children of Israel most of that over which they disagree.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ce Coran révélé à Muħammad expose aux Israélites la plupart des sujets sur lesquels ils divergent et il dévoile leur déviance.","explicationEn":"76. This Qur’ān which was revealed to Muhammad (peace be upon him) relates to the Israelites most of what they differ in, and it exposes their deviances.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027076","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-75.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-77.html"},{"numVerset":77,"texteArabe":"وَإِنَّهُ لَهُدًى وَرَحْمَةٌ لِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ","tradPropre":"cependant qu'il est pour les croyants un guide et une miséricorde.","tradEn":"And indeed, it is guidance and mercy for the believers.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tandis qu’il est une guidée et une miséricorde pour les croyants qui mettent en pratique ce qu’il contient.","explicationEn":"77. And it is a guidance and mercy for the believers who practice what it has brought.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027077","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-76.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-78.html"},{"numVerset":78,"texteArabe":"إِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِي بَيْنَهُمْ بِحُكْمِهِ  وَهُوَ الْعَزِيزُ الْعَلِيمُ","tradPropre":"Ton Seigneur décidera certes entre eux par Son jugement; et Il est le Tout Puissant, le Sage.","tradEn":"Indeed, your Lord will judge between them by His [wise] judgement. And He is the Exalted in Might, the Knowing.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, ton Seigneur jugera le Jour de la Résurrection avec équité entre les gens, qu’ils soient croyants ou mécréants. Il fera ensuite miséricorde au croyant et châtiera le mécréant. Il est le Puissant à qui personne ne peut tenir tête et le Connaisseur de toute chose, Celui qui distingue toujours les adeptes du vrai des adeptes du faux.","explicationEn":"78. O Messenger, your Lord will decide between the people, believers and disbelievers, on the day of judgment through His just judgment. He will have mercy on the believer and punish the disbeliever, and He is the Mighty who will take retribution from His enemies, with nobody to overpower Him, the Knowing to whom the truthful is not unclear from the liar.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027078","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-77.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-79.html"},{"numVerset":79,"texteArabe":"فَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ  إِنَّكَ عَلَى الْحَقِّ الْمُبِينِ","tradPropre":"Place donc ta confiance en Allah, car tu es de toute évidence dans la vérité et le bon droit.","tradEn":"So rely upon Allāh; indeed, you are upon the clear truth.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Remets t’en à Allah et compte sur Lui pour toutes tes affaires car tu détiens certainement la vérité explicite.","explicationEn":"79. So trust in Allah, and rely on Him in all your affairs. You are on the clear truth.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027079","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-78.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-80.html"},{"numVerset":80,"texteArabe":"إِنَّكَ لَا تُسْمِعُ الْمَوْتَىٰ وَلَا تُسْمِعُ الصُّمَّ الدُّعَاءَ إِذَا وَلَّوْا مُدْبِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Tu ne peux faire entendre les morts ni faire entendre l'appel aux sourds quand ils s'enfuient en tournant le dos.","tradEn":"Indeed, you will not make the dead hear, nor will you make the deaf hear the call when they have turned their backs retreating.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, tu n’as pas le pouvoir de faire entendre ceux dont les cœurs sont morts à cause de leur mécréance ni de faire entendre ton message à ceux qui ont perdu l’ouïe parce qu’ils se détournent de toi.","explicationEn":"80. O Messenger, you cannot make the dead whose hearts have died to their disbelief in Allah hear, nor can you make those who have lost their hearing hear what you are calling them towards when they return turning away from you.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027080","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-79.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-81.html"},{"numVerset":81,"texteArabe":"وَمَا أَنْتَ بِهَادِي الْعُمْيِ عَنْ ضَلَالَتِهِمْ  إِنْ تُسْمِعُ إِلَّا مَنْ يُؤْمِنُ بِآيَاتِنَا فَهُمْ مُسْلِمُونَ","tradPropre":"Et tu ne peux non plus guider les aveugles hors de leur égarement. Tu ne feras entendre que ceux qui croient en Nos versets et se soumettent.","tradEn":"And you cannot guide the blind away from their error. You will only make hear those who believe in Our verses so they are Muslims [i.e., submitting to Allāh].","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tu n’as pas non plus le pouvoir de guider ceux qui sont aveugles face à la vérité. Ne t’attriste donc pas pour eux et ne t’afflige pas car ta prédication ne sera accueillie que par ceux qui croient en Nos signes et se soumettent aux ordres d’Allah.","explicationEn":"81. And you are not one to guide those whose eyes are blind to the truth, so do not grieve over them and tire yourself. Only those will listen to your call who believe in our verses, because they submit to the orders of Allah.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027081","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-80.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-82.html"},{"numVerset":82,"texteArabe":"۞ وَإِذَا وَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ أَخْرَجْنَا لَهُمْ دَابَّةً مِنَ الْأَرْضِ تُكَلِّمُهُمْ أَنَّ النَّاسَ كَانُوا بِآيَاتِنَا لَا يُوقِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Et quand la Parole tombera sur eux, Nous leur ferons sortir de terre une bête qui leur parlera; les gens n'étaient nullement convaincus de la vérité de Nos signes [ou versets].","tradEn":"And when the word [i.e., decree] befalls them, We will bring forth for them a creature from the earth speaking to them, [saying] that the people were, of Our verses, not certain [in faith].","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> A la fin des temps, lorsque l’Heure sera sur le point de sonner.","explicationUnanime":"Lorsque leur châtiment sera inéluctable et qu’il sera confirmé à cause de leur obstination à mécroire et à désobéir, Nous leur manifesterons alors un des Signes Majeurs de l’Heure qui est la bête qui sortira de terre et leur parlera dans leur langue. Elle leur dira que les gens ne croyaient pas aux versets révélés à Notre Prophète.","explicationEn":"82. When the punishment becomes binding and established for them, due to their disbelief and sins, and the worst of people remain, I shall take out for them near to the Final Hour one of its greatest signs, which is a creature from the earth which will speak to them with what they understand that the people did not believe My verses which were revealed to My Prophet.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027082","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-81.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-83.html"},{"numVerset":83,"texteArabe":"وَيَوْمَ نَحْشُرُ مِنْ كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ فَوْجًا مِمَّنْ يُكَذِّبُ بِآيَاتِنَا فَهُمْ يُوزَعُونَ","tradPropre":"Et le jour où Nous rassemblerons, de chaque communauté, une foule de ceux qui démentaient Nos révélations, et qu'ils seront placés en rangs.","tradEn":"And [warn of] the Day when We will gather from every nation a company of those who deny Our signs, and they will be [driven] in rows","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi le Jour où Nous rassemblerons de chaque communauté certains de ses notables qui démentaient nos versets. Nous les alignerons des premiers jusqu’aux derniers puis ils seront trainés afin de rendre des comptes.","explicationEn":"83. O Messenger, remember the day I shall gather from each of the nations a group from amongst them the leaders who used to disbelieve in our ayaat, so they can precede their followers to the fire...the first group will be held until the last group of leaders are gathered and then they will be led to the reckoning.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027083","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-82.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-84.html"},{"numVerset":84,"texteArabe":"حَتَّىٰ إِذَا جَاءُوا قَالَ أَكَذَّبْتُمْ بِآيَاتِي وَلَمْ تُحِيطُوا بِهَا عِلْمًا أَمَّاذَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"puis, quand ils seront arrivés, [Allah] dira: «Avez-vous traité de mensonges Mes signes sans les avoir embrassés de votre savoir? Ou que faisiez-vous donc?»","tradEn":"Until, when they arrive [at the place of Judgement], He will say, \"Did you deny My signs while you encompassed them not in knowledge, or what [was it that] you were doing?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"On continuera de les trainer et parvenus au lieu où ils rendront des comptes, Allah les réprimandera en leur disant: Avez-vous démenti Mes versets prouvant Mon Unicité et contenant Mes lois sans vous être assurés qu’ils sont faux? Quels furent vos critères pour leur accorder du crédit ou les démentir?","explicationEn":"84. And their being led will continue until when they come to the place of their reckoning, Allah will say to them rebukingly: “Did you deny my signs which proved my Oneness and which comprised my sacred law, whilst you did not have proper knowledge to judge them to be false and disbelieve in them, or what was it that you were doing: believing or denying?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027084","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-83.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-85.html"},{"numVerset":85,"texteArabe":"وَوَقَعَ الْقَوْلُ عَلَيْهِمْ بِمَا ظَلَمُوا فَهُمْ لَا يَنْطِقُونَ","tradPropre":"Et la Parole leur tombera dessus à cause de leurs méfaits. Et ils ne pourront rien dire.","tradEn":"And the decree will befall them for the wrong they did, and they will not [be able to] speak.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Le châtiment s’abattra sur eux parce que leur mécréance et leur démenti des versets d’Allah les ont rendus injustes. Ils ne pourront pas plaider leur cause car ils en seront incapables et leurs arguments seront invalides.","explicationEn":"85. And the punishment will befall them due to their disbelieving in Allah and denying His ayahs. They will not speak to defend themselves due to their inability and the falsity of their proofs.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027085","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-84.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-86.html"},{"numVerset":86,"texteArabe":"أَلَمْ يَرَوْا أَنَّا جَعَلْنَا اللَّيْلَ لِيَسْكُنُوا فِيهِ وَالنَّهَارَ مُبْصِرًا  إِنَّ فِي ذَالِكَ لَآيَاتٍ لِقَوْمٍ يُؤْمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"N'ont-ils pas vu qu'en vérité, Nous avons désigné la nuit pour qu'ils y aient du repos, et le jour pour voir? Voilà bien des preuves pour des gens qui croient.","tradEn":"Do they not see that We made the night that they may rest therein and the day giving sight? Indeed in that are signs for a people who believe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ces dénégateurs n’ont-ils pas vu que Nous avons fait en sorte qu’ils dorment la nuit et que durant le jour, ils sont capables de voir afin de vaquer à leurs occupations. Cette mort et cette ressuscitation répétées sont assurément des signes clairs adressés à des gens croyants.","explicationEn":"86. Do these deniers of the resurrection not see that I made the night so that they can rest in it through sleep, and I made the day bright for them so that they can see therein and then hasten towards their work? In that repeated death and the rising after it are proofs for the resurrection after death.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027086","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-85.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-87.html"},{"numVerset":87,"texteArabe":"وَيَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ فَفَزِعَ مَنْ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَنْ فِي الْأَرْضِ إِلَّا مَنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ  وَكُلٌّ أَتَوْهُ دَاخِرِينَ","tradPropre":"Et le jour où l'on soufflera dans la Trompe, tous ceux qui sont dans les cieux et ceux qui sont dans la terre seront effrayés, - sauf ceux qu'Allah a voulu [préserver]! - Et tous viendront à Lui en s'humiliant.","tradEn":"And [warn of] the Day the Horn will be blown, and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will be terrified except whom Allāh wills. And all will come to Him humbled.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, rappelle-toi du Jour où l’ange soufflera le second souffle dans la Trompe. Tous ceux qui peupleront les Cieux et la Terre seront effrayés, sauf ceux qu’Allah aura exceptés par faveur de Sa part. Ce jour-là, toutes les créatures seront obéissantes et soumises à Allah.","explicationEn":"87. O Messenger, remember: the day in which the angel appointed to blow the trumpet a second time will blow, then everyone in the heavens and everyone on earth will be terrified except whom Allah has excluded from being terrified, as a grace from Him. And all the creation of Allah will come to him on that day, in obedience and with humility.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027087","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-86.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-88.html"},{"numVerset":88,"texteArabe":"وَتَرَى الْجِبَالَ تَحْسَبُهَا جَامِدَةً وَهِيَ تَمُرُّ مَرَّ السَّحَابِ  صُنْعَ اللَّهِ الَّذِي أَتْقَنَ كُلَّ شَيْءٍ  إِنَّهُ خَبِيرٌ بِمَا تَفْعَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et tu verras les montagnes - tu les crois figées - alors qu'elles passent comme des nuages. Telle est l'œuvre d'Allah qui a tout façonné à la perfection. Il est Parfaitement Connaisseur de ce que vous faites!","tradEn":"And you see the mountains, thinking them motionless, while they will pass as the passing of clouds. [It is] the work of Allāh, who perfected all things. Indeed, He is Aware of that which you do.","noteUnique":"<strong>Précision exégétique :</strong> Possible allusion à la rotation de la terre, comme semble l’indiquer la suite du verset. L’immense majorité des exégètes situe néanmoins ce verset dans le contexte de l’au-delà et des bouleversements qui accompagneront le Jour de la résurrection.","explicationUnanime":"Tu verras ce jour-là les montagnes que tu croiras immobiles alors qu’en réalité, elles se déplaceront aussi vite que les nuages. C’est ainsi qu’Allah les fait se déplacer. Il sait le mieux ce que vous faites. Rien de vos œuvres ne Lui échappe et Il vous rétribuera selon leur nature.","explicationEn":"88. And you will see mountains on that day thinking them to be firm without moving, but they will in fact move like clouds move. It is the doing of Allah, for He is the one who makes them move. He is Aware of what you do. None of your actions are hidden from Him and He shall reward you for them.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027088","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-87.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-89.html"},{"numVerset":89,"texteArabe":"مَنْ جَاءَ بِالْحَسَنَةِ فَلَهُ خَيْرٌ مِنْهَا وَهُمْ مِنْ فَزَعٍ يَوْمَئِذٍ آمِنُونَ","tradPropre":"Quiconque viendra avec le bien aura bien mieux, et ce jour-là, ils seront à l'abri de tout effroi.","tradEn":"Whoever comes [at Judgement] with a good deed will have better than it, and they, from the terror of that Day, will be safe.","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Quiconque se présentera le Jour de la Résurrection muni de foi et de bonnes œuvres aura comme récompense le Paradis et Allah l’épargnera de la terreur du Jour de la Résurrection.","explicationEn":"89. On the Day of Judgement, whoever brings faith and good deeds will gain paradise and will be safe from the horrors of that day due to Allah granting them that safety.","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027089","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-88.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-90.html"},{"numVerset":90,"texteArabe":"وَمَنْ جَاءَ بِالسَّيِّئَةِ فَكُبَّتْ وُجُوهُهُمْ فِي النَّارِ هَلْ تُجْزَوْنَ إِلَّا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Et quiconque viendra avec le mal... alors ils seront culbutés le visage dans le Feu. N'êtes-vous pas uniquement rétribués selon ce que vous œuvriez?»","tradEn":"And whoever comes with an evil deed - their faces will be overturned into the Fire, [and it will be said], \"Are you recompensed except for what you used to do?\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Tandis que celui qui se présentera muni de mécréance et de péchés aura comme punition le Feu et tous y seront jetés le visage le premier. On leur dira en même temps en guise de réprimande et de vexation: Ne recevez-vous pas la rétribution que vous méritez pour votre mécréance et votre désobéissance dans le bas monde?","explicationEn":"90. And whoever comes with disbelief and sins, for them will be the hellfire in which they will be thrown face first. It will be said to them by way of rebuke and humiliation: “Are you being requited except for the disbelief and the sins you used to commit?”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027090","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-89.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-91.html"},{"numVerset":91,"texteArabe":"إِنَّمَا أُمِرْتُ أَنْ أَعْبُدَ رَبَّ هَاذِهِ الْبَلْدَةِ الَّذِي حَرَّمَهَا وَلَهُ كُلُّ شَيْءٍ  وَأُمِرْتُ أَنْ أَكُونَ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ","tradPropre":"«Il m'a été seulement commandé d'adorer le Seigneur de cette Ville (la Mecque) qu'Il a sanctifiée, - et à Lui toute chose - et il m'a été commandé d'être du nombre des Musulmans,","tradEn":"[Say, O Muḥammad], \"I have only been commanded to worship the Lord of this city, who made it sacred and to whom [belongs] all things. And I am commanded to be of the Muslims [i.e., those who submit to Allāh]","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Ô Messager, dis-leur: Il ne m’a été ordonné que d’adorer le Seigneur de la Mecque, la cité qu’Allah a rendue sacrée. Aucune effusion de sang ne doit donc y avoir lieu, personne n’y doit être traité injustement, aucun gibier ne doit y être chassé et aucun arbre ne doit y être coupé. Allah, exalté soit-Il, possède toute chose et il m’a été ordonné de me soumettre à Lui, en Lui obéissant.","explicationEn":"91. O Messenger! Say to them: “I have only been commanded to worship the Lord of this city (Makkah) which He has sanctified, so no blood should be shed in it, nor should anyone be oppressed in it, nor should its game be hunted or trees cut. And to Him belongs the authority over everything. I have also been commanded to be from those who submit to Allah in obedience to Him.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027091","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-90.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-92.html"},{"numVerset":92,"texteArabe":"وَأَنْ أَتْلُوَ الْقُرْآنَ  فَمَنِ اهْتَدَىٰ فَإِنَّمَا يَهْتَدِي لِنَفْسِهِ  وَمَنْ ضَلَّ فَقُلْ إِنَّمَا أَنَا مِنَ الْمُنْذِرِينَ","tradPropre":"et de réciter le Coran». Quiconque se guide, c'est pour lui-même en effet qu'il se guide. Et quiconque s'égare..., alors dis: «Je ne suis que l'un des avertisseurs».","tradEn":"And to recite the Qur’ān.\" And whoever is guided is only guided for [the benefit of] himself; and whoever strays - say, \"I am only [one] of the warners.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Il m’a également été ordonné de réciter le Coran aux gens. Ceux parmi eux qui suivront sa guidée et le mettront en pratique en tireront bénéfice pour eux-mêmes tandis que ceux qui s’égareront, dévieront de ce qu’il enseigne, le rejetteront et ne le mettront pas en pratique, dis-leur: Je ne suis qu’un avertisseur qui vous met en garde contre le châtiment d’Allah et je n’ai pas le pouvoir de vous guider","explicationEn":"92. And I have been commanded to recite the Qur’ān to people; whoever is guided by it and implements its teachings, his guidance will benefit him. But whoever deviates from its teachings, rejects them and does not implement them, say to him: “I am only one of the warners; I warn you of the punishment of Allah. and your guidance is not in my hands.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027092","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-91.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-27-verset-93.html"},{"numVerset":93,"texteArabe":"وَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ سَيُرِيكُمْ آيَاتِهِ فَتَعْرِفُونَهَا  وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ","tradPropre":"Dis: «Louange à Allah! Il vous fera voir Ses preuves, et vous les reconnaîtrez». Ton Seigneur n'est pas inattentif à ce que vous faites.","tradEn":"And say, \"[All] praise is [due] to Allāh. He will show you His signs, and you will recognize them. And your Lord is not unaware of what you do.\"","noteUnique":"","explicationUnanime":"Dis également, ô Messager: Louange à Allah pour Ses bienfaits innombrables. Il vous montrera Ses signes dans vos propres personnes, dans le Ciel, dans la Terre ainsi que dans votre subsistance et vous les reconnaitrez d’une manière qui vous conduira à accepter la vérité. Ton Seigneur n’est pas inattentif à ce que vous faites. Il en a plutôt connaissance, rien ne Lui échappe et Il vous rétribuera en conséquence.","explicationEn":"93. Say - O Messenger: “All praise belongs to Allah for His innumerable blessings. He will show you His signs in the horizons and in yourselves; you will recognise them such that they will lead you to submitting to the truth. And your Lord is not neglectful of your actions; He is watching over them, none of them are hidden from Him and He will requite you for them.”","precisionConsensus":"","texteLaurierPerso":"","miracle":null,"codeAudio":"027093","lienPrecedent":"sourate-27-verset-92.html","lienSuivant":"sourate-28-verset-1.html"}]};